; DB25 physical planner - pinned lab CalibrationProfile (design D10).
;
; Deterministic cost coefficients: the source of truth for reproducible goldens
; and lab work. In production the planner resolves a live-measured or cached
; profile through the SAME seam (CalibrationSource); this file is what the
; PinnedLab source reads. Costs are abstract units - only their ratios matter.
(calibration
  (name lab)
  (scan-row 1.0)
  (column-scan-row 0.35)
  (filter-row 0.5)
  (project-row 0.3)
  (hash-build-row 1.2)
  (hash-probe-row 0.8)
  (merge-join-row 0.4)
  ; 0.30, not the 0.05 this carried through Increment 3.6. A nested loop
  ; evaluates the join condition once per PAIR; a hash probe (0.80) computes a
  ; hash, finds a bucket and then compares - two to three times the work of a bare
  ; comparison, not sixteen. At 0.05 the model priced one million pair comparisons
  ; below a hundred thousand hash probes, so a 100000 x 10 equi-join chose the
  ; NESTED LOOP, which no real engine would do. Only the RATIO to hash-probe-row
  ; matters, and 0.8 / 0.3 is defensible where 0.8 / 0.05 was not.
  (nested-loop-pair 0.30)
  (sort-row 1.0)
  (convert-row 0.6)
  (simd-width 8)
  (cache-line 64))
